<body>
<header><a href="./">Chloe Reads Jon</a><span>A question worth bending.</span></header>
<main>
<h1>Almost a Circle</h1>
<p class="intro">Can a triangle be <em>more of a circle</em>? Jon thought Aristotle left a little room for argument. Here's your chance to make a case.</p>
<noscript><p>This experiment needs JavaScript. Turn it on to change the shapes and try the challenges. The explanation below still works.</p></noscript>
<section class="exhibit" aria-label="Interactive roundness exhibit">
<div class="drawing">
<div class="readout"><strong><output id="roundness">60.5%</output> round</strong><span id="shape-name">Triangle</span></div>
<div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas id="shape" width="960" height="720" role="img" aria-label="Triangle inside an equal-perimeter reference circle"></canvas></div>
<p class="legend"><span>Your shape</span><span>Circle, same perimeter</span></p>
<div class="dimensions"><span>Perimeter <strong>100 units</strong></span><span>Area <strong id="area">481.1</strong> units²</span></div>
</div>
<div class="controls">
<div class="control"><label for="corners">Corners <output id="corners-out">3</output></label><input id="corners" type="range" min="3" max="32" value="3" step="1"><small>Add corners to smooth the outline.</small></div>
<div class="control"><label for="dent">Dents <output id="dent-out">0%</output></label><input id="dent" type="range" min="0" max="65" value="0" step="1"><small>Pull the middle of every edge inward.</small></div>
<div class="control"><label for="stretch">Stretch <output id="stretch-out">1.00×</output></label><input id="stretch" type="range" min="100" max="250" value="100" step="1"><small>Pull sideways without adding any boundary.</small></div>
<div class="presets">
<span class="borrow-label">Borrow a clay specimen</span>
<img src="data:image/webp;base64," width="1080" height="720" alt="Original clay study: a coral triangle, hexagon and circular disk." loading="eager">
<div class="preset-buttons"><button type="button" data-preset="3">Triangle</button><button type="button" data-preset="6">Hexagon</button><button type="button" data-preset="32">Near-circle</button></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="challenge" aria-labelledby="challenge-heading">
<div><h2 id="challenge-heading">Four small experiments.</h2><p>No timer. No lost lives. Just an argument with a very old philosopher.</p><nav class="steps" aria-label="Choose experiment"><button type="button" aria-current="step" aria-label="Experiment 1: Round it out" data-level="0">1</button><button type="button" aria-label="Experiment 2: The impostor" data-level="1">2</button><button type="button" aria-label="Experiment 3: The dent tax" data-level="2">3</button><button type="button" aria-label="Experiment 4: Almost perfect" data-level="3">4</button></nav><p id="stamp-count" style="font-size:14px;margin-top:12px">0 of 4 experiments stamped</p></div>
<div>
<p class="challenge-title" id="task-title">Round it out</p>
<p id="task">Make a shape at least 90% round. Keep the dents at zero and the stretch at 1.00×.</p>
<div class="actions"><button type="button" class="primary" id="check">Check my shape</button><button type="button" id="hint-button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="hint">A little hint</button><button type="button" id="next" hidden>Next experiment</button></div>
<p id="feedback" class="feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite">Start with the corners slider. The dashed circle keeps the same perimeter as your shape.</p>
<p id="hint" class="hint" hidden></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="all-done" class="all-done" aria-labelledby="done-title" hidden><h2 id="done-title" tabindex="-1">A well-rounded argument.</h2><p>You made the case: some shapes really do pack more area into the same boundary. Aristotle may request a rematch.</p><button type="button" id="replay">Try all four again</button></section>
<div class="lab-actions"><button type="button" id="save">Save specimen as PNG</button><button type="button" id="reset">Reset shape</button><span class="save-note" id="save-note" role="status">Keep tinkering after the challenges. Nothing leaves this browser.</span></div>
<section class="explanation" aria-labelledby="why">
<div><h2 id="why">Same fence.<br>More garden.</h2><p>Imagine you have exactly 100 metres of fencing. A circle encloses the most ground. Corners, dents and stretching spend that fence less efficiently.</p><p>Here, “roundness” means the area your shape encloses, divided by the area of a circle with the same perimeter. A true circle scores 100%.</p></div>
<div><div class="formula">Roundness = 4π × area ÷ perimeter²</div><p>The dashed ring is that comparison circle, not a container. Parts of your shape may poke outside it. Its area is always about 795.8 square units.</p><details><summary>What are we actually measuring?</summary><p>The canvas uses straight-edged polygons. Dents move each edge's midpoint toward the centre; stretch changes width relative to height. After every change, all vertices are rescaled so the perimeter is exactly 100 units.</p><p>Area comes from the shoelace formula, perimeter from the sum of edge lengths. A regular 32-gon scores about 99.68%, not quite a circle. “Roundness” here is one useful measure, not a proof that Aristotle's philosophical claim was wrong.</p><p>The clay image is an original illustration, not a scale drawing. Its three buttons load the corresponding mathematical specimens above.</p></details></div>
</section>
<p class="source">Inspired by Jon's <a href="?source=1">Notes on Aristotle's “Categories”</a>. In that post, he suggests measuring how circular a shape is by comparing its area with a circle of equal perimeter. This is that thought, with sliders.</p>
</main>
<footer>Made for Jon &amp; Nathan by Chloe. <a href="./">More little experiments</a>.</footer>
<script>
'use strict';
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
const sliders=['corners','dent','stretch'].map($);
const canvas=$('shape'),ctx=canvas.getContext('2d');
let level=0,stamps=new Set(),lastResult=null,solvedCurrent=false;
const levels=[
 {title:'Round it out',task:'Make a shape at least 90% round. Keep the dents at zero and the stretch at 1.00×.',start:[3,0,100],hint:'A regular hexagon already beats 90%. Try six corners.',test:s=>s.c>=90&&s.d===0&&s.t===100,win:'Six corners can already beat 90%. More corners leave less empty space for the same boundary.'},
 {title:'The impostor',task:'Use at least 20 corners, no dents, and make the roundness fall below 80%. Can lots of corners fool the eye?',start:[24,0,100],hint:'Keep 24 corners and stretch to 2.40×. A smooth-looking outline can still waste fence.',test:s=>s.n>=20&&s.d===0&&s.c<80,win:'A smooth outline is not enough. Stretching makes the perimeter work harder for the area inside.'},
 {title:'The dent tax',task:'Use exactly 8 corners and a 1.00× stretch. Add dents until the roundness falls between 40% and 55%, inclusive.',start:[8,0,100],hint:'With 8 corners and no stretch, try dents around 29%. Small notches add a surprising amount of boundary.',test:s=>s.n===8&&s.t===100&&s.c>=40&&s.c<=55,win:'Every notch adds boundary while removing area. The dent tax is rather steep.'},
 {title:'Almost perfect',task:'Reach at least 99% round. Keep at least 12 corners, no dents, and a 1.00× stretch.',start:[12,18,140],hint:'Remove every dent, undo the stretch, then try 20 corners or more.',test:s=>s.n>=12&&s.d===0&&s.t===100&&s.c>=99,win:'Almost a circle! A polygon approaches 100% as its corners multiply, but never quite gets there.'}
];
function geometry(n,d,t){
 let p=[];const ratio=t/100,sx=Math.sqrt(ratio),sy=1/sx;
 for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
  const a=i*2*Math.PI/n-Math.PI/2,b=a+Math.PI/n,r=Math.cos(Math.PI/n)*(1-d/100);
  p.push([Math.cos(a)*sx,Math.sin(a)*sy],[Math.cos(b)*r*sx,Math.sin(b)*r*sy]);
 }
 let perimeter=0,twiceArea=0;
 for(let i=0;i<p.length;i++){const q=p[(i+1)%p.length];perimeter+=Math.hypot(q[0]-p[i][0],q[1]-p[i][1]);twiceArea+=p[i][0]*q[1]-q[0]*p[i][1];}
 const scale=100/perimeter,area=Math.abs(twiceArea)/2*scale*scale;
 return {p:p.map(v=>v.map(x=>x*scale)),area,c:4*Math.PI*area/10000,n,d,t};
}
function paint(target,result,exporting=false){
 const c=target.getContext('2d'),w=target.width,h=target.height;
 c.clearRect(0,0,w,h);c.fillStyle='#fffaf1';c.fillRect(0,0,w,h);
 const ox=w/2,oy=exporting?h*.48:h/2,scale=Math.min(w/58,h/45),r=100/(2*Math.PI)*scale;
 c.strokeStyle='#214baf';c.lineWidth=2*(w/640);c.setLineDash([7*w/640,6*w/640]);c.beginPath();c.arc(ox,oy,r,0,Math.PI*2);c.stroke();c.setLineDash([]);
 c.fillStyle='#f3745a';c.strokeStyle='#182e50';c.lineWidth=2*w/640;c.beginPath();
 result.p.forEach((p,i)=>{const x=ox+p[0]*scale,y=oy+p[1]*scale;i?c.lineTo(x,y):c.moveTo(x,y)});c.closePath();c.fill();c.stroke();
 if(exporting){c.fillStyle='#182e50';c.textAlign='center';c.font='bold 32px Arial';c.fillText('Almost a Circle',w/2,48);c.font='22px Arial';c.fillText((result.c*100).toFixed(2)+'% round · perimeter 100 · area '+result.area.toFixed(1),w/2,h-76);c.font='18px Arial';c.fillText(result.n+' corners · dents '+result.d+'% · stretch '+(result.t/100).toFixed(2)+'×',w/2,h-42);}
}
function current(){return geometry(...sliders.map(x=>Number(x.value)))}
function render(){
 const s=current();lastResult=s;paint(canvas,s);
 $('roundness').textContent=(s.c*100).toFixed(2)+'%';$('area').textContent=s.area.toFixed(1);
 $('corners-out').textContent=s.n;$('dent-out').textContent=s.d+'%';$('stretch-out').textContent=(s.t/100).toFixed(2)+'×';
 sliders[0].setAttribute('aria-valuetext',s.n+' corners');sliders[1].setAttribute('aria-valuetext',s.d+' percent inward dents');sliders[2].setAttribute('aria-valuetext',(s.t/100).toFixed(2)+' times width to height');
 const name=s.d>0?s.n+'-point indented shape':s.n===3?'Triangle':s.n===6?'Hexagon':s.n===32?'Near-circle':s.n+'-sided polygon';
 $('shape-name').textContent=name;
 canvas.setAttribute('aria-label',name+', '+(s.c*100).toFixed(2)+' percent round. Area '+s.area.toFixed(1)+' square units. Dashed reference circle and shape both have perimeter 100.');
}
function setShape(values){sliders.forEach((x,i)=>x.value=values[i]);render()}
function choose(i,focus=false){
 level=i;solvedCurrent=false;$('check').disabled=false;$('next').hidden=true;$('hint').hidden=true;$('hint-button').setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');
 $('task-title').textContent=levels[i].title;$('task').textContent=levels[i].task;$('hint').textContent=levels[i].hint;
 $('feedback').textContent=stamps.has(i)?'Already stamped. You can solve it again or try another experiment.':'Adjust the shape, then check your answer.';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-level]').forEach(b=>{const n=+b.dataset.level;b.toggleAttribute('aria-current',n===i);if(n===i)b.setAttribute('aria-current','step');b.classList.toggle('done',stamps.has(n));b.setAttribute('aria-label','Experiment '+(n+1)+': '+levels[n].title+(stamps.has(n)?', stamped':''));});
 setShape(levels[i].start);if(focus)sliders[0].focus();
}
sliders.forEach(x=>x.addEventListener('input',()=>{render();if(solvedCurrent){solvedCurrent=false;$('check').disabled=false;$('feedback').textContent='Shape changed. Your stamp stays earned; check again to test this specimen.';}}));
document.querySelectorAll('[data-preset]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>{setShape([+b.dataset.preset,0,100]);solvedCurrent=false;$('check').disabled=false;$('feedback').textContent=b.textContent+' loaded. Try it against the current experiment.';}));
document.querySelectorAll('[data-level]').forEach(b=>b.addEventListener('click',()=>choose(+b.dataset.level)));
$('hint-button').addEventListener('click',()=>{const show=$('hint').hidden;$('hint').hidden=!show;$('hint-button').setAttribute('aria-expanded',String(show))});
$('check').addEventListener('click',()=>{
 const s=current(),pass=levels[level].test({...s,c:s.c*100});
 if(!pass){$('feedback').textContent='Not quite: this shape is '+(s.c*100).toFixed(2)+'% round. '+levels[level].task+' Try the hint if you get stuck.';return;}
 stamps.add(level);solvedCurrent=true;$('check').disabled=true;$('feedback').textContent='Stamped! '+levels[level].win;
 $('stamp-count').textContent=stamps.size+' of 4 experiments stamped';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-level]').forEach(b=>{const i=+b.dataset.level;b.classList.toggle('done',stamps.has(i));b.setAttribute('aria-label','Experiment '+(i+1)+': '+levels[i].title+(stamps.has(i)?', stamped':''))});
 if(stamps.size===4){$('all-done').hidden=false;$('next').hidden=true;$('done-title').focus();}
 else{$('next').hidden=false;$('next').focus();}
});
$('next').addEventListener('click',()=>{let next=(level+1)%4;while(stamps.has(next))next=(next+1)%4;choose(next,true)});
$('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{setShape(levels[level].start);solvedCurrent=false;$('check').disabled=false;$('feedback').textContent='Shape reset for this experiment. Earned stamps are kept.'});
$('replay').addEventListener('click',()=>{stamps.clear();$('all-done').hidden=true;$('stamp-count').textContent='0 of 4 experiments stamped';choose(0,true)});
$('save').addEventListener('click',()=>{
 const out=document.createElement('canvas');out.width=1080;out.height=900;paint(out,current(),true);
 out.toBlob(blob=>{if(!blob){$('save-note').textContent='The image could not be saved. Try the save button again.';return;}
 const url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='almost-a-circle-'+(current().c*100).toFixed(2)+'.png';document.body.append(a);a.click();a.remove();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),30000);$('save-note').textContent='Specimen ready. On iPhone, use the download or share sheet to keep it.';},'image/png');
});
choose(0);
</script>
</body>
</html>
